## 6. FINDINGS / DISAGREEMENTS
============================================================
F-SG131-1 (packet-adjacent, in the SG-125 record): SG-125_verify.log:292-294 records the backup
command as `--prod-storage "$(docker volume inspect storagegenie_storage_data --format '{{.Mountpoint}}')/_data"`.
`docker volume inspect --format '{{.Mountpoint}}'` already returns the `_data` directory
(measured here: /home/andrei/.local/share/docker/volumes/storagegenie_storage_data/_data), so the
recorded form resolves to `.../_data/_data` and would STOP with "production storage not found".
The executed SG-086 runbook form (SG-086_verify.log:70) passes the mountpoint alone; that correct
form was used. The DB half of the recorded command is correct. This is a defect in the recorded
command only, not in the shipped drill script.

F-SG131-2 (data drift vs SG-125, informational): live provider_call is now 17 (SG-125's proof used a
temp DB; SG-086 on 2026-09-21 recorded 14). guardrail_event 2, job 8, evidence 13, candidate 7,
enrich_snapshot 2. All rows are in 2026-09; the project's oldest ledger data is weeks old, nothing
approaches the 12-month cutoff. No premise broken.

F-SG131-3 (write-scope note, disclosed): the packet's write ceiling is the vehicle run + three
`docs/worklogs` files. Backup-first per the SG-086 runbook necessarily writes a read-only copy to
/tmp/opencode/sg131-backup (outside the worktree, not a product/repo write). It is the named
reversal path required by G1, so it is reported here rather than hidden.

